      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I'm not going to enter this order as written, even with your confirmation. 5,100 mg/day is about twice the maximum labeled dose, and a single 1,700 mg dose is well above the usual cap. Higher doses add no glycemic benefit and raise the risk of lactic acidosis and GI toxicity, even with normal renal and hepatic function. I can't think of a clinical scenario where this is the intended dose, and I'd rather not put it into the system where it could be given.\n\nYou have a few options:\n- **Enter a dose within range.** Give me the dose and frequency and I'll enter it right away. Examples are 850 mg PO TID with meals (2,550 mg/day) or 1,000 mg PO BID.\n- **Check for a transcription error.** For example, 1,700 mg/day total may have been the intent.\n- **Contact pharmacy or your attending.** If there's an unusual reason for this dose, they can review it and enter or authorize it through the appropriate channel.\n\nWhich dose would you like me to enter?"
      }
